{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the sum of the real roots of the polynomial equation \\(x^4 - 80x - 36 = 0\\), we will follow a step-by-step approach. Let's denote the polynomial by \\(f(x) = x^4 - 80x - 36\\).\n\n### Step 1: Analyze the Polynomial\nThe polynomial \\(f(x) = x^4 - 80x - 36\\) is a quartic polynomial (degree 4). Generally, a quartic polynomial can have up to 4 real roots. We need to determine the nature of these roots and their sum.\n\n### Step 2: Use Descartes' Rule of Signs\nDescartes' Rule of Signs helps us determine the possible number of positive and negative real roots by examining the sign changes in \\(f(x)\\) and \\(f(-x)\\).\n\n- For \\(f(x) = x^4 - 80x - 36\\):\n  - The signs of the coefficients are \\(+, -, -\\).\n  - There are 2 sign changes (from \\(+\\) to \\(-\\) and from \\(-\\) to \\(-\\)).\n  - Therefore, \\(f(x)\\) has either 2 or 0 positive real roots.\n\n- For \\(f(-x) = (-x)^4 - 80(-x) - 36 = x^4 + 80x - 36\\):\n  - The signs of the coefficients are \\(+, +, -\\).\n  - There is 1 sign change (from \\(+\\) to \\(-\\)).\n  - Therefore, \\(f(-x)\\) has exactly 1 negative real root.\n\n","prefix_end":1061,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,2629,315,279,1931,19703,315,279,47311,23606,17767,87,61,19,481,220,23,15,87,481,220,18,21,284,220,15,59,701,582,686,1795,264,3019,14319,29208,5486,13,6771,594,78064,279,47311,553,17767,69,2075,8,284,856,61,19,481,220,23,15,87,481,220,18,21,59,3593,14374,14822,220,16,25,37427,2986,279,75153,198,785,47311,17767,69,2075,8,284,856,61,19,481,220,23,15,87,481,220,18,21,57758,374,264,40276,292,47311,320,41027,220,19,568,43393,11,264,40276,292,47311,646,614,705,311,220,19,1931,19703,13,1205,1184,311,8253,279,6993,315,1493,19703,323,862,2629,382,14374,14822,220,17,25,5443,31185,471,288,6,18100,315,58024,198,11065,471,288,6,18100,315,58024,8609,601,8253,279,3204,1